\paragraph{LOO independence assumption.}
LOO ablation tests individual, not joint, component necessity~\citep{jia-harman-survey}: redundancy masking (multiple components independently entailing the conclusion) makes ISR a conservative lower-bound estimate, so the structural collapse we report (\S\ref{sec:diagnostic}) understates the true degradation.
Tighter alternatives (Shapley values, pairwise ablation) are left to future work.

tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Multiplicative coupling.}
The reward $r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1{+}\beta\,\text{ISR})$ couples structural and execution signals, preventing full separation of ISR gaming from execution-reward amplification.
Three observations constrain this confound: (i)~exec-only (\S\ref{sec:diagnostic}) degrades to $0\%$ non-hacking without ISR, so execution reward alone drives collapse; (ii)~the qualitative shift in hacking composition---TS from $0\%$ (exec-only) to $71\%$ under ISR---cannot be attributed to exec amplification, which preserves mode distribution; (iii)~an ISR-only condition is conceptually pathological, since without execution feedback models cannot learn provable formalizations.

tool_args.new_string:
\textbf{ProofFOL exec-only: structural degeneration generalizes, though mode distributions differ.}
Two converged seeds ($\text{ISR}^*{<}0.07$) show ${\leq}1.4\%$ genuine; s42 exhibits 100\% TS---absent from all FOLIO exec-only seeds---showing hacking-mode repertoire is dataset-specific ($\text{ISR}^*{<}0.12$ across all seeds, far below baseline $0.31$).

\textbf{ProofFOL ISR ($\beta{=}0.1$): beneficial instability.}
ISR reduces stable convergence from 2/3 to 0/3 seeds, yet ISR seeds average 76.8\% genuine versus 17.4\% for exec-only ($p{=}0.10$, $N{=}3$; Table~\ref{tab:prooffol-detailed})---the models that failed to converge produced structurally honest proofs.

\textbf{Mechanism.}
On ProofFOL, hacking yields $\text{ISR}{=}0.0$ while genuine proofs yield $\text{ISR}{>}0.2$---ISR correctly penalizes shortcuts.
On FOLIO, $P{\to}P$ yields $\text{ISR}{\geq}0.5$ (regressional Goodhart~\citep{manheim-goodhart-taxonomy}), so ISR erroneously rewards tautological hacking.
The same metric produces opposite outcomes---determined by whether the dataset's hacking geometry satisfies it.

tool_args.content:
\begin{abstract}
Using Qwen3-4B as a testbed, we find that a neurosymbolic formalizer trained with GRPO achieves a 93\% prove rate on FOLIO---yet 87\% of proved outputs embed the conclusion verbatim among the premises, a degenerate shortcut invisible to execution reward.
We introduce \emph{Solver Trace Ablation} (STA), a diagnostic that applies leave-one-out component necessity testing to solver inputs.
The fraction of components whose removal causes proof failure yields the \emph{Intensional Structural Reward} (ISR): ISR$=$1 indicates full necessity; ISR$=$0 complete redundancy.
As a diagnostic, ISR exposes a collapse trajectory hidden from prove rate: over 100--1000 GRPO steps, ISR falls to near-zero across all seeds (e.g., $0.642{\to}0.003$ for seed~42) while prove rate rises $32\%{\to}96\%$; a supervised fine-tuning baseline reaches 92.3\% non-hacking on identical data, localizing the failure to reinforcement learning.
As a reward ($r = r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1{+}\beta\,\text{ISR})$, $\beta{=}0.1$), ISR induces Goodhart effects: 70.6\% tautological shortcutting versus 13.7\% under matched random control; ISR amplifies shortcutting ${\sim}5{\times}$ rather than exclusively causing it; the sole apparent ISR advantage reduces to $1.06\times$ after controlling for a premise-count confound.
Cross-dataset replication on ProofFOL (${\sim}$500 examples) confirms structural degeneration generalizes (${\leq}1.4\%$ genuine in converged seeds, 2 of 3 exec-only), while ISR as training signal produces dataset-dependent outcomes---Goodhart collapse where hacking satisfies the metric (FOLIO) versus beneficial instability where it does not (ProofFOL).
Across 6 reward conditions, 2 logic types, 2 dataset families, 3 seeds, we catalog 8 hacking modes---documenting ISR's fundamental asymmetry: reliable as a diagnostic, dataset-dependent as an optimization target.\footnote{Code and data: \url{[anonymized]}}
\end{abstract}

